.TH "rbc::PDF" 3tcl 0\&.8\&.1 "rbc" "Upgraded Tcl/Tk9\&.0-ready RBC package"
.SH NAME
rbc::PDF - Commands in namespace rbc::PDF
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBcget\fP \fIoption\fP
.br
\fBconfigure\fP \fIoption\fP
.br
\fBconfigure\fP \fIoption value ?option value \&.\&.\&.?\fP
.br
\fBoutput\fP \fI?fileName? ?option value \&.\&.\&.?\fP
.br
.SH "GRAPH PDF PDF COMMAND"
.PP
The PDF component exports a single-page PDF 1\&.4 document directly, without Cairo, Ghostscript or another PDF
library\&. It is available on graph, barchart, stripchart and polar widgets, independently of the screen
renderer\&. Each widget has its own PDF settings, separate from SVG and PostScript settings\&.
.SH "GENERATING PDF"
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
\&.g pdf output plot\&.pdf
\&.g pdf output plot\&.pdf -width 16c -height 12c -decorations yes
set bytes [\&.g pdf output]
set channel [open copy\&.pdf wb]
puts -nonewline $channel $bytes
close $channel
.fi
.RE
.PP
Without a filename, output returns a binary Tcl bytearray\&. File output uses binary translation\&. Prefix a
dash-leading filename with a directory, for example \&./-plot\&.pdf\&. There is no -- separator\&. Rendering and
text validation finish before the destination is opened\&. An I/O failure can still leave a partial file\&.
.SH "PDF OPTIONS"
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
┌──────────────────────┬─────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Option               │ Default │ Description                                                                         │
├──────────────────────┼─────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ -width distance      │ 0       │ Non-negative width, in pixels or Tk screen-distance units\&. Zero uses the graph      │
│                      │         │ width\&.                                                                              │
│ -height distance     │ 0       │ Non-negative height, in pixels or Tk screen-distance units\&. Zero uses the graph     │
│                      │         │ height\&.                                                                             │
│ -decorations boolean │ 1       │ Include backgrounds and relief borders\&. False uses white backgrounds; labels, axes  │
│                      │         │ and symbols remain visible\&.                                                         │
│ -embedfonts boolean  │ 1       │ Embed native fonts and Unicode mappings\&. False uses standard PDF fonts with         │
│                      │         │ Windows-1252 text\&.                                                                  │
└──────────────────────┴─────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
.fi
.RE
.PP
Dimensions are stored as integer pixels, like SVG options\&. The export lays out the graph at those dimensions
and converts the resulting coordinates to PDF points using the display's horizontal pixels-per-inch value (the scale used by Tk screen distances)\&.
One PDF point is 1/72 inch\&. Physical distances are therefore subject to Tk's integer-pixel rounding\&. With
zero dimensions, the current widget size is used, or its requested size before layout\&. The page fits the
graph; there are no paper-size, printer-margin, landscape or multipage options in this version\&.
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
\&.g pdf configure -width 16c -height 12c
puts [\&.g pdf cget -width]
puts [\&.g pdf configure -decorations]
\&.g pdf configure -width 0 -height 0
.fi
.RE
.PP
Query descriptors contain {option name class default current}\&. PDF options do not use the Tk option
database\&. Invalid option/value lists leave settings unchanged\&. Validated output options remain configured
even if later rendering or file writing fails\&. Export restores screen geometry and does not resize the widget\&.
.SH "SUPPORTED CONTENT AND LIMITATIONS"
.PP
Lines, error bars/bands, axes, grids, standard geometric symbols, arrows, polygon and arc markers, backgrounds,
borders and legends use vector paths\&. Elliptical arcs use cubic Bezier approximations\&. Export uses full source
geometry rather than screen-decimated traces\&. Solid fill opacity uses PDF transparency; stipples use vector
tiling patterns\&. Image tiles and photo markers embed RGB images with soft masks for alpha\&. Resources are
reused within each document\&. This first version writes uncompressed streams, so image-heavy PDFs can be large\&.
.PP
By default, text uses embedded fonts and Unicode mappings for searching and copying\&. Mathematical symbols, Greek letters,
superscripts and subscripts are supported when an installed font supplies their glyphs\&. Tk 9's per-character
font actual query supplies the actual family, size and style, including fallback characters; the standard
Tk font command must be available\&. Character positions, advances, rotation and shadows retain Tk's layout\&.
Font lookup uses GDI on Windows and Fontconfig on X11, independently of Cairo\&. Core-X11 legacy fonts are
matched to scalable equivalents; if needed, Fontconfig selects another outline font containing the character\&.
If a legacy X11 font measures a missing glyph as zero, PDF uses the fallback glyph advance to avoid overlap\&.
Such substitution, synthesized styles and platform font matching can differ from the exact screen appearance\&.
.PP
TrueType outlines (including OpenType/TrueType and faces in collections) and ordinary name-keyed OpenType/CFF
fonts are embedded\&. Complete font programs are stored once per document, without subsetting or compression,
so PDFs can be larger than before\&. Font embedding permissions are respected\&. Variable fonts, CID-keyed CFF,
CFF2 and color/bitmap-only fonts are not supported\&. A missing glyph or unsupported/restricted font reports an
error before an output file is opened; unsupported characters are not silently replaced\&. PostScript font/color
maps are not used\&. PDF remains version 1\&.4; Unicode page text does not require PDF 2\&.0\&.
.PP
To produce a smaller document without embedded font programs:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
\&.g pdf output compact\&.pdf -embedfonts no
\&.g pdf configure -embedfonts yes
.fi
.RE
.PP
This mode substitutes standard Helvetica, Times or Courier faces, retaining bold/italic styles and Tk text
positions\&. The PDF viewer supplies the fonts, so appearance can differ\&. Text is limited to Windows-1252;
unsupported characters produce an error asking to enable -embedfonts, before opening the destination\&.
Superscript/subscript or mathematical characters outside that repertoire require embedding\&. This setting
is independent of SVG's -embedfonts, which defaults to false\&.
.PP
Non-photo Tk images use the same black/white off-screen capture technique as SVG; custom image types with
destination-dependent drawing may differ\&. Mapped window markers embed their current native pixels as raster
images\&. Hidden or unmapped windows are omitted, and the exporter does not run the event loop\&. Process pending
display work before exporting window markers\&. Native capture availability and visibility constraints apply\&.
.SH COMMANDS
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBcget\fR (::rbc::PDF)
.RE
.PP
Queries a PDF option\&. Dimensions are returned as integer pixels\&.
.RS 4n
\fBcget\fP \fIoption\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
option
PDF configuration option\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
Current option value\&.
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBconfigure\fR (::rbc::PDF)
.RE
.PP
Queries or atomically updates PDF settings\&. See \fIPDF options\fP\&.
.RS 4n
\fBconfigure\fP \fIoption\fP
.br
\fBconfigure\fP \fIoption value ?option value \&.\&.\&.?\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.RE
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
Option descriptors when querying, otherwise nothing\&.
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBoutput\fR (::rbc::PDF)
.RE
.PP
Exports a single-page PDF\&. See \fISupported content and limitations\fP\&.
.RS 4n
\fBoutput\fP \fI?fileName? ?option value \&.\&.\&.?\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
fileName
Optional destination; prefix dash-leading names with \&./\&.
.TP
option
Optional PDF configuration option\&.
.TP
value
New option value, retained after validation\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
Binary PDF bytearray without a filename, otherwise nothing\&.


